<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Command: Showcase, Ford Class</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY&gt;&lt;P&gt;Desperate to sell its product to foreign markets and secure an inflow of currency to buoy its central bank, Moscow has invested in several illicit trade routes to North Korea, Iran, and others willing to deify US and European sanctions. Unwilling to risk war with Russia but unhappy that their sanctions are being avoided, the US and NATO are doing everything that they possibly can, short of direct combat, to aggravate Russia.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;One of these economic lifelines’ funnels grain and oil through Angola into central and parts of southern Africa. Of course, this development has not gone unnoticed and the government in Luanda has faced mounting pressure to renounce any agreements with Russia. Three days ago, on the eve of a much-anticipated announcement, the Angolan President was killed in a vehicle accident and several key government officials disappeared. The resulting chaos has unleashed increasing violence throughout the country particularly in the capitol. Pandora’s box has been opened and a state of civil war now exists in Angola.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;While most western countries have initiated evacuation of embassy and non-combatant personnel (NEO, Non-combatant Evacuation Operation), Russia is flying in ‘peacekeepers’ to secure its investment and infrastructure. The British and French have temporarily secured the Luanda International Airport to enable multiple NEO, and the US has dispatched CSG 12 (Carrier Strike Group), centered on the new aircraft carrier &lt;EM&gt;USS Gerald R. Ford&lt;/EM&gt; to the area, diverting it from a long-planned visit to Brazil.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Note&lt;/STRONG&gt;: 
&lt;P&gt;At the time of writing (late 2022) the USN had not decided on the future air group configuration for it’s Carrier Air Wing (CVW). There were several options available in open-source media and probably several others under consideration. The three available in this scenario focus on the number of F-35C available and are as follows:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Maximum&lt;/STRONG&gt;: 20x F-35, 12x F/A-18E Block III, 12x F/A-18F Block III&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Medium&lt;/STRONG&gt;: 14x F-35, 12x F/A-18E Block III, 16x F/A-18F Block III&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Minimum&lt;/STRONG&gt;: 10x F-35, 12x F/A-18E Block III, 20x F/A-18F Block III&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In each case there are 44 strike-fighters. These are augmented by EA-18G (5, 7, or 9) EW aircraft, E-2D (4, 5, or 5) AEW aircraft, and MQ-25 (9, 8, or 6) refueling UAV. All told there will be 62 fixed wing aircraft plus 14 rotary-wing, which do not change between options, and 2 Carrier On-board Delivery (COD) CVM-22B Osprey. &lt;STRONG&gt;Total of 78 aircraft&lt;/STRONG&gt;.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You will need to go to the &lt;STRONG&gt;Special Actions&lt;/STRONG&gt; menu and chose which one you wish to play the scenario with within the first 15 minutes of the scenario.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;</ScenDescription>
